      "problem": "What is the cardinality of $H\\times K$ for $H={1,2,3,…,9}$ and $K={x,y}?$",
      "worked_solution": "For any two finite sets $H$ and $K,$ the cardinality of $H\\times K$ is\n\n$$\n|H\\times K|=|H|\\cdot |K|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|H\\times K| & =|H|\\cdot |K| \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
